== New data, bounded attribution
The oracle emits previously unreported native F4 total/stair observations around the unchanged solve_visit and each actual callback. Checked arithmetic separates observed callback windows from outside windows, retains Result-refusal observations with a caller-held owner, and rejects reused owners without overwriting prior data. Replay checks metadata arithmetic and visitor/attempt/callback consistency. Older records without the optional field remain readable. #raw("[pcc:unverified]")

The provider uses process-wide relaxed atomic counters for incomplete native classes. Concurrent work can contaminate windows; separate loads are not a transaction. Valid-looking differences do not establish isolation or rule out a full wrap. Outside callback windows are not exclusive solver costs. Stair is already included in native total. Inclusive is another view of its parts, not an additional charge. Price remains null, complete coverage false and both provider-overflow and solver-attribution qualifications false.

