= Consistency controls and remaining qualification
== Four new controls
1. A real nested F4 call inside a visitor produces positive callback-native work. Outside-plus-callback observations reconcile to inclusive; tampered outside counts fail metadata checks.
2. Invalid input retains a rejected Result state with zero callbacks. Not-called data is distinct, and reusing the same owner cannot overwrite it.
3. Synthetic backwards, inconsistent-subset and overflow differences become unavailable rather than zero or wrapped exact values. This does not qualify every underlying provider wrap/race.
4. Replay binds the native attempted state to visitor presence and callback diagnostics. Older records without the field still replay for correctness; missing cost data is not free. #raw("[pcc:unverified]")

A producer can fabricate consistent metadata. The new checks are not independent execution proof or complete operation accounting. Returned means Result::Ok, including incomplete/capped solver reports, not successful scalar recovery. A held owner keeps Result-refusal observations, but the upper producer run API can still discard its local ledger on Err. No durable failed-process/crash/resume claim follows.

== Root arithmetic remains an explicit gap
The solver-tree root multiplication field and callback root multiplication field are two executed phases, not duplicate views. Both are partial. Source review finds linear and p2 shortcuts in poly_roots_fp_counted_until that omit the supplied multiplication accumulator; inverse/addition/control work is also incomplete. The p2 shortcut is outside current PKM p>11 inputs; linear cases remain relevant. This step leaves the core unchanged and records the gap instead of claiming full root coverage. A later core change requires new source-bound affected validation. #raw("[pcc:unverified]")

Legacy solve_excluding_callbacks clocks subtract named callback phase timers, not all wrapper/observer work. No denominator, timing comparison, complete price or GAE result was introduced. The field_ops_total provider's configured thread/process behavior remains unchanged. Full symbolic/substitution/matrix/logical/root/native work, guards, metadata/serialization, memory, whole-process/journal and qualified runtime/resume remain open.

